{
  "title": "The Half-Orc | Someone Opened the Gate With His Knife | Full Fantasy Film",
  "description": "A work of fiction. Every nation and place in this story is invented. All people and animals in this film are AI-generated. No real animals were harmed.<br><br>Harrowmere is a timber town, the last wall before the red steppe, and Kael is the only half-orc on its gate watch. One night a hand in the dark cuts the rope that holds the gate bar. The Varga riders come through on their Ironbacks, armoured lizards as tall as a man, and Kael holds the old stone bridge while the townsfolk cross, until the riders&apos; war-leader, Torga, lowers her axe and looks at him as if she knows him.<br><br>By morning the town has found a knife in the gate rope, and it is Kael&apos;s. Lord Marshal Corwin sends him out of the walls under war law, and Kael walks into the Red Sands with Isolde Varn&apos;s waterskin, her knife, and a gold coin stamped with an elk&apos;s head that he picked out of the mud by the gate and showed to no one.<br><br>Out on the sands wait a worm of living stone beneath the dunes, an orc camp that trusts him even less than the town did, a black Ironback no one has ever ridden, and Old Ruin, the giant of the herd, with a broken horn. Then one night riders under no banner come for the camp, and an arrow they leave behind carries the same elk&apos;s head as his coin. Someone is paying to push the town and the steppe into war, and the only one who has stood on both sides is the man neither side will trust.<br><br>The Half-Orc is an original cinematic story inspired by the orcneas, a word for monsters that appears once in the Old English poem Beowulf. At line 112 the poet lists &quot;eotenas ond ylfe ond orcneas&quot;: giants, elves and orcneas, and never says what the orcneas looked like. Harrowmere, the Varga, the Ironbacks, the Gravel Wyrm and the House of the Grey Elk are invented, as is every people, beast, law and character in the film.<br><br>Chapters<br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zBu7YoN5-GM\">0:00</a> Prologue: The Open Gate<br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zBu7YoN5-GM&amp;t=164\">2:44</a> Chapter One: Exiled<br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zBu7YoN5-GM&amp;t=362\">6:02</a> Chapter Two: The Red Sands<br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zBu7YoN5-GM&amp;t=630\">10:30</a> Chapter Three: The Camp of the Varga<br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zBu7YoN5-GM&amp;t=793\">13:13</a> Chapter Four: The Night Raid<br><br>Written &amp; directed by Gilded Myth Pictures<br>Cast: Kael, a half-orc of the gate watch · Torga, war-leader of the Varga riders · Grukka, an old orc woman of the camp · Morzhul, chieftain of the Varga · Isolde Varn, captain of the Harrowmere riders · Corwin, the Lord Marshal · Hollis, captain of the gate · The hooded man, name unknown<br>Music: YouTube Audio Library<br><br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/fantasyfilm\">#fantasyfilm</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/epicfantasy\">#epicfantasy</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/halforc\">#halforc</a>",
